From b43777dbee06c17aa58c5abb0f18d99ae28de35a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:07:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: enforce first-party compiler warnings without blocking
 dependencies

Keep Rust workspace and explicit native first-party warnings fatal. External
native compilation uses the toolchain warning defaults. Verify clean code,
a fatal first-party warning, and a visible nonfatal dependency-policy warning.

Red: dependency-warning-policy-red.log rejects the dependency fixture.
Green verification is retained in the task execution record.

Apply the same warning policy to V8 build configuration, which otherwise adds
its own -Werror. Preserve every warning flag and all third-party C++ sources.
The action-level regression checks the production V8 compile arguments.
Red: hosted Windows GNU jobs reject Abseil deprecations through V8 -Werror.
Focused emitted-patch verification is retained in the task execution record.

Consolidate follow-up corrections while preserving the final implementation:
- zzzz-0050-v8-analysis-test-size.patch

Original focused red/green records remain in the owning task evidence.
Fresh emitted-queue verification is a separate acceptance gate.
